ref 17592186233174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e6c66f6-6133-59f6-a79d-0cbf1615accf" :question/math-academy-id "q-113665" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {x}^{20}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=20$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{20}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{20+1}}{20+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{21}}{21}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{21}}{21}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{21}}{21})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{21}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{21})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{21}\\cdot 21{x}^{20} & = \\\\ {x}^{20}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233175 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7949e7bf-09d1-5ce9-ac3c-0d7f26b2e6c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-113670" :question/problem "Calculate $F(x)$ given that $f(x)={x}^{17}$ and ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe apply the power rule with $n=17$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{17}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{17+1}}{17+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{18}}{18}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{18}}{18}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{18}}{18})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{18}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{18})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{18}\\cdot 18\\,{x}^{17} & = \\\\ {x}^{17}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234186 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "48cc16d0-0280-564d-bcf3-e481ad8d20ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-66126" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "If we write the integrand as a power of $x$, we have ${x}^{0}=1.$ Therefore, we can use the power rule with $n=0$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{0+1}}{0+1}+C \\\\  & =x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ 1+0 & = \\\\ 1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb47b292-deba-58b8-a79e-0386e8ea55e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-71121" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {x}^{10}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=10$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{10}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{10+1}}{10+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{11}}{11}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{11}}{11}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{11}}{11})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{11}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{11})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{11}\\cdot 11{x}^{10} & = \\\\ {x}^{10}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503848 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d6ad986-0c26-5cd6-9cd3-04a7be56d694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{6}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503846} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec8b324-f032-547f-97d9-6c73f80f4440" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503850} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe67df0-46d1-5acd-abf6-e732a8688e8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503855} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b1f0d3-bec7-598d-ba2e-a3f438f06ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7x^{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503868} {:answer/id #uuid "fa59a2a3-a8ed-5b0b-abda-91a9bba04e9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{7}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa59a2a3-a8ed-5b0b-abda-91a9bba04e9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{7}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503875} :answer-field/id #uuid "b67f2104-8e47-50cd-b752-fad1aa17e5ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503867}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4194dc2e-82ad-5109-91f4-d383eed4b18e" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=6$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{6+1}}{6+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{7}}{7}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{7}}{7}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{7}}{7})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\cdot 7{x}^{6} & = \\\\ {x}^{6}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503851 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b9bd22-8b41-542b-82ba-62e400af4a02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503842} {:answer/id #uuid "0b7b7de0-eaf8-57d9-8475-c23f72194dd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x^{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503844} {:answer/id #uuid "a5bb73e6-3ec8-51dd-ad3b-1cd6d6243b7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503862} {:answer/id #uuid "b52194ac-60ec-5ec7-91b2-c8a58426c3e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503866} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d839d9-d182-5a2a-8ca4-8961f79ffaae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{8} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01b9bd22-8b41-542b-82ba-62e400af4a02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503842} :answer-field/id #uuid "88eaa69f-9171-51b9-9926-45e937a2ad36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4fc55d29-07c8-58f3-8bc8-d1223d0589d0" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Include the arbitrary constant of integration." :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=7$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{7+1}}{7+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{8}}{8}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{8}}{8}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{8}}{8})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{8})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 8{x}^{7} & = \\\\ {x}^{7}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503854 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "081fa2f5-42b3-5c04-80c9-10a003c271a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x^{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503843} {:answer/id #uuid "4a21e63a-5ffd-51d5-a90e-548e77d4bab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{6}}{6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503849} {:answer/id #uuid "7015537d-a311-57e0-815f-dece8e7c2eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503853} {:answer/id #uuid "84bc4aa5-c9e8-54dc-9352-f633e5591d8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503857} {:answer/id #uuid "dd56a3a8-a755-5234-b43f-e287021340e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a21e63a-5ffd-51d5-a90e-548e77d4bab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{6}}{6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503849} :answer-field/id #uuid "51200684-dca8-5045-9aea-e16255caa7bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "74bb6151-9d7e-5db4-9d07-e87c336986aa" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=5$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{5+1}}{5+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{6})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 6{x}^{5} & = \\\\ {x}^{5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19401952-b969-5a9f-9750-1720c3ea9602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{9}}{9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503845} {:answer/id #uuid "3d942c43-21e5-5ec4-b609-785240316ce4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x^{7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503847} {:answer/id #uuid "7ff916ab-3641-575c-b8ab-d8ce83a4174b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503856} {:answer/id #uuid "90147ce6-5ad4-56fc-aa26-0fc98c813215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{8}}{8} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503861} {:answer/id #uuid "ce201103-531a-5e28-bbe3-329fc7ec8063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19401952-b969-5a9f-9750-1720c3ea9602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{9}}{9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503845} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe44896c-83fc-509b-862e-d8c3138397c3" :answer-field/key